# Copy to .env.local for development. NONE of these are required to run srsly:
# with an empty file the app works fully in local-guest mode — reading, lookups, EPUBs,
# flashcards and the lesson tree all run with no account and no network calls to anyone.

# ── Sync (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set BOTH or NEITHER. `supabaseEnabled` in lib/supabase/client.ts is the switch, and with
# it off there is no auth and no metering — exactly as the app behaved before sync existed.
# Create a project, run supabase/schema.sql, then see supabase/SETUP.md for the redirect
# URLs, which are what a deployed sign-in needs and localhost does not.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Passage generation (optional, and DELIBERATELY UNSET IN PRODUCTION) ───────
# Generation is bring-your-own-key: learners paste their own Anthropic key in Settings and
# are billed directly by Anthropic, roughly a cent a passage. These two are the OPERATOR's
# fallback, for local development only.
#
# On a public deployment, leave them EMPTY. Anonymous sign-ins are enabled and
# GUEST_AI_LIMIT (supabase/schema.sql) rations five operator-funded passages per guest — so
# a key set here means every visitor can spend five passages on your card. Unset, the app
# shows its no-key state pointing at Settings, which is the designed behaviour.
#
# SRSLY_API_KEY exists because Claude Code sets ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='' in its own environment,
# which would otherwise blank the key during development. Either name works.
SRSLY_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Text-to-speech (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, /api/tts returns 501 and lib/speech.ts falls back to the browser's own
# speech synthesis — free, offline, and the path most installs take. With it, audio is
# generated by OpenAI and billed to you, so the same public-deployment warning applies.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Development only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serves canned content instead of calling a model, so the reading pipeline can be worked on
# without spending tokens (lib/server/stubContent.ts). It fires on this explicit flag alone
# and is never a fallback for a missing key: content a learner cannot tell apart from real
# output is what this codebase refuses everywhere else.
# SRSLY_STUB_AI=1
